{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And it shall be, if the wicked man deserves to be beaten.</b> With a resh [as] in בן נון. Another reading: בן. יקה, and the meaning is like בן בליעל. And so he was a son of the night. And he is liable. To beat him, in my opinion, [means] he struck his fellow." "<b>And the judge shall cause him to fall.</b> In the imperative [case], and likewise והכהו and והעד לפניו." "<b>According to the measure of his wickedness, in number.</b> The blows. It would appear to us that there is an offense for which one is given ten lashes, also twenty, and fewer and more, and the witness [is] 'according to his wickedness' — only not exceeding forty, were it not for the words of the received tradition, and it alone is the truth. And some say that the meaning of 'his wickedness' is in great or small blows, and all of them by the count of forty."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is cryptic throughout; 'son of the night' and the 'יקה' reference are rendered literally without expansion. The letter-name reference 'בחיר״ק' appears to be a cryptographic or abbreviation notation, rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:45.126449955Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}